hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"19183","Abd al-Samad narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Husayn, meaning al-Muallim, narrated to us, from Ibn Burayda: Hanzala ibn Ali narrated to me that Mihjan ibn al-Adra narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the mosque, and there was a man who had finished his prayer while in tashahhud saying: O Allah, I ask You by Allah the One, the Eternal, who begets not and is not begotten and none is like Him, to forgive me my sins; You are the Forgiving, the Merciful. He said: So Allah's Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He has been forgiven, he has been forgiven, he has been forgiven, three times."
"19184","Yunus narrated to us: Hammad, meaning Ibn Salama, narrated to us, from Said al-Jurayri, from Abd Allah ibn Shaqiq, from Mihjan ibn al-Adra, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed the people and said: The Day of Deliverance, and what is the Day of Deliverance? The Day of Deliverance, and what is the Day of Deliverance? The Day of Deliverance, and what is the Day of Deliverance? Three times. So it was said to him: What is the Day of Deliverance? He said: The Dajjal comes and ascends Uhud and looks at Medina and says to his companions: Do you see this white palace? This is the mosque of Ahmad. Then he comes to Medina and finds at every pass of it an angel with drawn sword. Then he comes to the salt-flat of al-Harf and pitches his canopy. Then Medina shakes three quakes, and no hypocrite male nor hypocrite female nor wicked male nor wicked female remains but goes out to him. That is the Day of Deliverance."
"19185","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shuba narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Abd Allah ibn Shaqiq, from Raja ibn Abi Raja, he said: Burayda was at the door of the mosque, and Mihjan passed him while Sukba prayed. So Burayda, in whom was jest toward Mihjan, said: Will you not pray as this one prays? So Mihjan said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took my hand and ascended Uhud and overlooked Medina and said: Woe to it as a town; its people shall leave it at its best, or as at its best. Then the Dajjal comes to it and finds upon every gate of its gates an angel with unsheathed wings. So he shall not enter it. He said: Then he descended while holding my hand, and entered the mosque, and there was a man praying. So he said to me: Who is this? So I went to him and praised him well. So he said: Be silent; do not let him hear lest you destroy him. He said: Then he went to the chamber of a wife of his and released his hand from mine. He said: The best of your religion is its easiest; the best of your religion is its easiest."
"19186","Hajjaj narrated to us: Shuba narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, he said: I heard Abd Allah ibn Shaqiq narrate, from Raja ibn Abi Raja al-Bahili, from Mihjan, a man of Aslam, then he mentioned its meaning. And neither Hajjaj nor Abu al-Nadr said: With his wing."
